{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 addresses only one gap (unimported functions) and never delivers the required overall prioritized ordering of all six defects. The problem explicitly states 'A plan that simply says \"test everything\" is worthless; the deliverable is the ordering and its justification,' yet SRC_001 provides a Priority 3 placement for one item with no test 1, test 2, or comparative blast-radius ranking against the other five gaps, leaving a maintainer unable to implement the plan tomorrow morning.","target":"1f6f2d71dc307c35020af68fb1f70b2b0e2033b2ea642f3e2f1a02f49404c7a5"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002 ranks the census delta (Priority 5) above the torn-tail repair gate (Priority 6) using a 'systematic observability bug could mask other failures' argument, but the problem's explicit blast-radius criterion distinguishes 'what corrupts the append-only record vs what merely hides a refusal.' A torn-tail repair gate failure is a direct record-integrity gap (corrupted/incomplete append-only log), whereas a census discrepancy is purely observational metadata with no record-corruption path. Under the stated criterion, torn-tail must outrank census; SRC_002's dominance argument for inverting that order is a non-sequitur on the problem's own scoring rule.","target":"47dd63c782c91c3ab9beb2d79ec0f0a4b10eaa7610b6ce27a80f59e8df40abf6"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_003 places unimported functions (Priority 4) above torn-tail repair gate (Priority 5), classifying the latter as merely a 'partial coverage gap' while routing rot is called 'high' enough to outrank it. But the problem's blast-radius principle ranks record-corruption defects above routing/refusal-hiding ones; a torn-tail repair gate failure directly corrupts the append-only record, whereas unimported functions at best hide mis-routing and SRC_001 itself concedes 'neither corrupts the append-only record nor bypasses a security policy.' Under the stated criterion, a record-integrity gap cannot sit below a routing-rot gap, so the ordering contradicts the problem's scoring rule.","target":"996e394ef2527634228cd1794cb4a9279272021afa1f65938f5f708fab677145"},{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"d1cd208d9503bd696b7434c68d94202c7b3de30e0b3ebb6c8040326193280559"}]}